Description: FactoryTalk View SE and ME HMI projects, runtime logs, alarm logs, audit trails, data logs, and global objects. Captures the engineering project (.ggfx displays, .HMI project metadata) and runtime artifact folders. This is the highest-value target in DFIR for OT environments: the HMI project files contain display logic and were the attack surface in CVE-2024-7513 (default INTERACTIVE group write to project folder). Bulletproof against locked files via AlwaysAddToQueue on critical artifacts.
Author: Raul B Netto (Cybolt DFIR)
Version: 1.1
Id: e69b3c0e-02d3-4c7b-9245-bcecf495e146
RecreateDirectories: true
Targets:
    -
        Name: FT View SE - HMI projects - Global Objects (.ggfx)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Documents\RSView Enterprise\SE\HMI projects\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.ggfx"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "Global Object display files. MFT timestamps reveal display modification. AlwaysAddToQueue: KAPE will raw-read these if the HMI server has them open. CVE-2024-7513 default INTERACTIVE write applies here."
    -
        Name: FT View SE - HMI projects - Project metadata (.HMI)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Documents\RSView Enterprise\SE\HMI projects\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.HMI"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "HMI project metadata files. AlwaysAddToQueue: critical for forensic timeline."
    -
        Name: FT View SE - HMI projects - All files (catch-all)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Documents\RSView Enterprise\SE\HMI projects\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        Comment: "Catch-all for any other files in the project (macros, parameter files, etc.) NOT AlwaysAddToQueue to keep secondary pass fast."
    -
        Name: FT View SE - HMI projects (legacy XP/2003 path)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Documents and Settings\All Users\Shared Documents\RSView Enterprise\SE\HMI Projects\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        Comment: "Legacy path on Windows XP / Server 2003 hosts."
    -
        Name: FT View SE - Data Log files (.DAT / .OBF)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Documents\RSView Enterprise\SE\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.DAT"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "SE data log binary files. Pair with .OBF index. Locked by HMI server during runtime -> AlwaysAddToQueue."
    -
        Name: FT View SE - Data Log files (.OBF index)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Documents\RSView Enterprise\SE\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.OBF"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "SE data log index files. Use FT View File Viewer to read. Locked by HMI server during runtime -> AlwaysAddToQueue."
    -
        Name: FT View ME - HMI projects (modern path)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Documents\RSView Enterprise\ME\HMI projects\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        Comment: "ME engineering projects (.mer sources)."
    -
        Name: FT View ME - Runtime logs on PC / MobileView / IPC
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Documents\RSView Enterprise\ME\Logs\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "ME runtime logs when running on Windows PC / MobileView / industrial PC. Contains M_Alarms (HISTORY.ALM), M_AuditTrails, M_DataLogs, Diagnostics. AlwaysAddToQueue: these are open by ME Station at runtime."
    -
        Name: FT View ME - Runtime logs on PanelView Plus 7/6
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Windows\Logs\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "ME runtime logs when running on PanelView Plus 7 or Plus 6 (Windows CE 6.0 embedded). Limited to \\\\Windows\\\\Logs on the device."
    -
        Name: FT View ME - Runtime logs on legacy PanelView (Storage Card)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Storage Card\Rockwell Software\RSViewME\Logs\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "ME runtime logs on legacy PanelView Plus / Compact / CE using the removable storage card."

# Documentation
# HMI project files (.ggfx, .HMI, .mer) on a FactoryTalk View server are the
# engineering source-of-truth for what the operator sees. Modifications outside
# of change windows are evidence of either unauthorized engineering or attacker
# tampering. ALWAYS preserve these files before any re-deploy or restore, with
# their original NTFS timestamps.
#
# Bulletproof notes:
#   - .ggfx and .HMI are the most likely files to be locked by the HMI server
#     during live triage. AlwaysAddToQueue forces KAPE to attempt a raw disk
#     read (via FTK Imager-style read) if the regular copy fails.
#   - The catch-all with mask "*" (without AlwaysAddToQueue) is a safety net
#     for project files we didn't anticipate.
#   - ME runtime logs are appended to constantly while the application is
#     running. AlwaysAddToQueue here is critical to capture the current
#     session's audit trail and alarm history before triage.
#
# View SE/ME log file types and their viewers:
#   SE DataLog     : .DAT + .OBF      (FT View File Viewer)
#   ME DataLog     : .LOG              (FT View File Viewer)
#   ME Alarm log   : HISTORY.ALM       (HMI Tag Alarm Log Viewer)
#   ME Audit trail : in M_AuditTrails\ (CSV exportable)
#   ME RecipePlus  : .RPP              (FT View File Viewer)
#
# References: Rockwell View SE User Guide, CISA ICSA-24-226-06 (CVE-2024-7513).
